<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50764" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱππό-καμπος</span></b> , ὁ,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>monster with horse's body
				and fish's tail</i>, on which the sea-gods rode, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				831
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑστήκει Ποσειδῶν χάλκεος, ἔχων ἱ.
					ἐν τῇ χειρί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					8.7.2
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>Im.</u>
				1.8
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> a small fish,
				<i>the sea-horse</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				2.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				14.20
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				12.362
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
